      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're probably looking for some rough-around-the-edges, no-good types that fit the bill. Here are a few archetypes for the street-level scum:\n\nThere's Vinnie \"The Bull\" LaRosa, a short-tempered, tattooed punk who runs the local corner store and collects protection money from the other bums. Then there's Ricky \"The Kid\" Martinez, a scrappy young hustler who's always looking for the next score, whether it's a stolen car or a mark to rob. You've also got Sal \"The Slick\" Esposito, a smooth-talking, fast-living con artist who's always spinning a new tale to get out of a tight spot. Then there's Jimmy \"The Knife\" O'Connor, a hulking, sociopathic thug who's always looking for a fight or a way to make a quick buck. And finally, there's Old Man Jenkins, a grizzled, one-eyed ex-con who just wants to be left alone, but is always happy to share his wisdom (and his booze) with the other misfits.",
